<title>USA: Universal Standard Medical Q4 loss rises.</title>
<headline>Universal Standard Medical Q4 loss rises.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTHFIELD, Mich. 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr  loss		  $0.62     loss	$ 0.05</p>
<p> Net  loss		  4,065     loss	   298</p>
<p> Revs			13,589		   15,881</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   6,538		    6,360</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q4 results include charge of $2.8 million for additional cost reduction and reengineering initiatives, including addition of key personnel and implementation of processing engineering.  </p>
<p>			YEAR</p>
<p> Shr loss		  $ 1.20     loss	 $0.15</p>
<p> Net loss		   7,751     loss	   981</p>
<p> Revs			57,564		   66,773</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   6,462		    6,404</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full name is Universal Standard Medical Laboratories Inc.</p>
<p>1996 full-year results include special charge of $5.3 million. For 1996, the net loss, before special charges, would have been $2.7 million or $0.41/shr.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
</text>
